{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515915-antagonist-and-enemies","id":1515915,"title":"Antagonist and enemies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-22T17:18:57-07:00","id":1515915,"title":"Antagonist and enemies","content":"They say that a story is only as good as its antagonists, I don't know if I agree, but I know that WOD has a lot of material for enemies, even if sometimes they are other playable supernaturals and humans, but that aside, I wish someone here invented it some antagonist for your chronicles, it doesn't have to be original, I just wanted to know if there's anything out of the ordinary Wyrm or Technocracy, what kind of ideas you had and how you handled them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T21:39:04-07:00","id":1515928,"title":"","content":"<b>Skywatch</b>, a witchhunter/Hunters Hunted style organization of UFO fanatics, conspiracy theorists, and self-described alien abduction survivors (actually victims of involuntary enchantment and ravaging) who hunt Changelings, believing them to be alien pod-people conducting a covert invasion of Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T21:58:07-07:00","id":1515929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515915-antagonist-and-enemies?p=1515928#post1515928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Skywatch</b>, a witchhunter/Hunters Hunted style organization of UFO fanatics, conspiracy theorists, and self-described alien abduction survivors (actually victims of involuntary enchantment and ravaging) who hunt Changelings, believing them to be alien pod-people conducting a covert invasion of Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are they Modus Operanti?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T22:34:14-07:00","id":1515930,"title":"","content":"How do you mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T00:08:58-07:00","id":1515931,"title":"","content":"I think in vampire, the things is that most antagonists are the result of player choice. Sure, some vampires might not like their sire or desire their territory, but it's the player's fault that anyone acts against them 90% of the time.<br /> <br /> In werewolf, yeah, monster of the week. Mage is a mixed bag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T03:56:43-07:00","id":1515938,"title":"","content":"On one session I used domestic monster hunters, and so with the baddest luck on dice roll I ever seen in my entire life they cut the head of tiger bastet with one axe chop.<br /> I used Orpheus group after players messed with ghosts, but this time PC outsmarted enemy protecting the Veil.<br /> List of enemies is enormous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T07:04:43-07:00","id":1515947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515915-antagonist-and-enemies?p=1515930#post1515930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean what kind of strategy they normally use to approach and capture/eliminate Changelings and if possible some possible interaction with other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T11:53:57-07:00","id":1515957,"title":"","content":"Mainly a lot of surveillance of individuals and locations (including Freeholds), trying to intervene in &quot;abductions&quot; (including newly emerging Changelings undergoing the chrysalis and people being enchanted), and trying to rescue and sometimes &quot;deprogram&quot; people who've been enchanted as servants of the Fey. Some of them will sometimes go as far as advocating and carrying out violence against &quot;the invaders&quot;. This is especially true for many of the members who were family or friends of people who were &quot;replaced&quot; by the Sidhe in 1969 or during the Reckoning, and for those whose lives were ruined by Ravaging. <br /> <br /> Inspirationally, they take a lot from the UFO and conspiracy subcultures of the 70s, 80s, and 90s. Especially parts of The X-Files (the characters known as The Lone Gunmen are a good example of some of them), and other things like Close Encounters of the Third Kind, Fire in the Sky, Invasion of the Body Snatchers, and the original V miniseries. <br /> <br /> One of their biggest threats against Changelings is that their very myopic and narrow world view, especially as it relates to all things Fey, gives them fairly high Banality ratings. <br /> <br /> They probably don't encounter other supernaturals very often, with the exception of things like Psychics and government Twilight Agents. However, it is possible that any of them encountering vampires or werewolves may mistake them for a &quot;new&quot; type of alien invaders. And again, because of the same mental state that gives them a high Banality, they are likely to remember any encounter with the Delirium from Werewolf as some sort of inhuman alien monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T12:29:24-07:00","id":1515958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515915-antagonist-and-enemies?p=1515957#post1515957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of their biggest threats against Changelings is that their very myopic and narrow world view, especially as it relates to all things Fey, gives them fairly high Banality ratings.</div> </div> </div> </div>How high? You mean high inside of humam standarts like 6 or 7 points of Banality, or something like the autumnal people (8 or higher)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T12:40:44-07:00","id":1515960,"title":"","content":"7 or 8 probably, with the truly committed/obsessed sometimes going as high as 9. Possibly 10 if you wanted one as a major antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T15:34:44-07:00","id":1515970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515915-antagonist-and-enemies?p=1515957#post1515957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They probably don't encounter other supernaturals very often, with the exception of things like Psychics and government Twilight Agents. However, it is possible that any of them encountering vampires or werewolves may mistake them for a &quot;new&quot; type of alien invaders. And again, because of the same mental state that gives them a high Banality, they are likely to remember any encounter with the Delirium from Werewolf as some sort of inhuman alien monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just a curiosity, but what would they say if one of the members had a late first change, awakened an avatar, or become a Hunter?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T22:44:42-07:00","id":1515988,"title":"","content":"If Awakened, their obsessiveness may lead to periods of mental illness or breakdown, possibly manifesting as Quiet or Derangement. (Probably not as a full blown Marauder, but that's always a possibility if you want.) Paranoia might lead to them becoming Orphans, but if found by other Awakened, they might find a place in groups like the Virtual Adepts, Sons of Ether, or Hollow Ones. Alternately, if they become members of the Akashic Brotherhood or Dreamspeakers, they might get the sort of therapy that would allow them to deal with past trauma and move forward in a more healthy direction. If found by the Technocracy, their mindset would fit in well with parts of the Void Engineers, at least once their idea that the government and other powers that be are part of the alien conspiracy is ... corrected. <br /> <br /> If one of them became a werewolf or other shifter, they'd probably go off the deep end rather quickly, questioning if they are still really themselves or just an alien replacement that thinks it is the person they were. The sort of Lost Cubs that the Valkenberg Foundation dealt with by keeping them locked up in very secure mental wards. <br /> <br /> The Imbued are/were kind of all over the place with their interpretations of what they and their enemies are. (I think there actually was a character in one of the Creed-books who was an AWOL soldier who believed monsters were aliens.) They'd probably just double down on their existing beliefs and paranoia. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T01:16:23-07:00","id":1516950,"title":"","content":"<b>The Magrath Family </b>Scottish Ferectori/Wyrm Cultist Clan who betrayed other clans to the English for noble, then political power.<br /> They are a Nineteenth Century predecessor to Pentax, purposefully purchasing corrupt, scandalous or disreputable companies to reputedly repair their reputations but in reality from pure irony.<br /> <br /> They are cross splat their current leader (in the 1860\u2019s) is ordained by the Wyrm and possesses rites that bestow psychic abilities as well as formori type powers that allows him to steal and use vitae, gnosis etc.<br /> He isn\u2019t intended to be a match for a Garou more a behind the scenes orchestrator but he can soak and heal lots of supernatural damage by transmitting it to enslaved supernatural linked to him by his rituals.<br /> Their main horror aspect are extensive formori breeding pits which they use as a private army in their areas of interest.<br /> <br /> They also target low level vampires, mage etc lure them in, corrupt them usually through a combination of Wyrm powers and often using captured neonate kindred blood to ghoul them, whilst keeping the childer in torpor.<br /> <br /> They make pacts with various factions selling their services in return for furthering their own interests, all the while they are secretly hunting the various supernaturals for their essential materials.<br /> (Currently they have a pact with the Prince of San Francisco to keep the Sabbat contained in the South, whilst the Camarilla deal with a Hungry Dead incursion), which serves their purpose in kidnapping Sabbat Neonates).<br /> <br /> They are careful to only attack the Garou on their terms and from a position of surprise, they avoid acting against vampire elders or established mage, unless in a position of secrecy and strength and only if the benefits are worth it.<br /> <br /> Their weakness - well firstly the are horribly Wyrm tainted so family members either hole up in their fortresses or travel via dark umbra paths on rare trips, they are like a beacon to the Garou and people with low levels of true faith. Mortals feel physically sick from just being near them for short periods of time, Garou and people with higher levels of True Faith almost frenzy when encountering them.<br /> <br /> So far the Fledgling Storm Eaters impact on the Middle Umbra has confused local Garous and spirit senses, in the West.<br /> <br /> Their activities have a huge impact on the local Shadowlands attracting spectres and spawning nihils, they also provoke a similar reaction in wraiths as those with higher true faith, they utilise various rites, sorcery and the low level True Magik to conceal this in the Middle Umbra as much as possible.<br /> <br /> They have already removed the presence of family members from their Hudson Bay operation as local Faithful discovered their presence and started to disrupt their business interests.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T01:37:51-07:00","id":1516953,"title":"","content":"<b>The Red Branch </b>A group of Dauntain and Kinain, aware of their nature using their banal powers and some sorcery for their own ends, originally from Ireland with Fenian links.<br /> <br /> Some members have migrated to America to escape Fianna, Kithain and the British armies attention.<br /> Recently made a pact with the Van Bell Family for protection in the Carolina\u2019s as they rather foolishly contracted a New York gang to steal an artefact which turned out to be owned by a kindred elder.<br /> <br /> <b>The Van Bells </b>Old enemy brought from other games, secretive, local Nephandus and his two sons, they serve very powerful outer dark gods and have a Jeepers Creepers type monster bound to their apple orchard chantry.<br /> <br /> These are my Cthulhu mythos type villains where most of the PCs activities are investigating their activities and stopping their minions.<br /> <br /> They have a gunslinger agent who whilst seemingly human is largely impervious to harm due to his body wide tattoos (he can be disrupted through pattern Magik).<br /> <br /> <b>The Eyes of Thoth </b>Egyptian order of enlightened mortals who want to free their lands from Colonial oppression and reclaim the stolen treasures of their heritage, the PCs have a lot of sympathy with them despite their interests often clashing (the orders knowledge doesn\u2019t extend to anything other than very basic supernatural lore so they do try and reclaim dangerous artefacts)<br /> <br /> <b>High Collar Man </b>Another favourite villain imported, the PCs have never worked out what he is other than at times he is completely murderous towards them whilst other times helps them for unknown reasons.<br /> <br /> He\u2019s actually an Erlking Thallain Grump with considerable command over travelling through the Dreaming and possibly the Middle Umbra, combat abilities and arts to rival a Garou and displays a high tolerance against Banality.<br /> <br /> Unsurprisingly his name comes from his always having his high colour up and a top hat to conceal his face.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T08:41:53-07:00","id":1516973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515915-antagonist-and-enemies?p=1516950#post1516950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Magrath Family </b>Scottish Ferectori/Wyrm Cultist Clan who betrayed other clans to the English for noble, then political power.<br /> They are a Nineteenth Century predecessor to Pentax, purposefully purchasing corrupt, scandalous or disreputable companies to reputedly repair their reputations but in reality from pure irony.<br /> <br /> They are cross splat their current leader (in the 1860\u2019s) is ordained by the Wyrm and possesses rites that bestow psychic abilities as well as formori type powers that allows him to steal and use vitae, gnosis etc.<br /> He isn\u2019t intended to be a match for a Garou more a behind the scenes orchestrator but he can soak and heal lots of supernatural damage by transmitting it to enslaved supernatural linked to him by his rituals.<br /> Their main horror aspect are extensive formori breeding pits which they use as a private army in their areas of interest.<br /> <br /> They also target low level vampires, mage etc lure them in, corrupt them usually through a combination of Wyrm powers and often using captured neonate kindred blood to ghoul them, whilst keeping the childer in torpor.<br /> <br /> They make pacts with various factions selling their services in return for furthering their own interests, all the while they are secretly hunting the various supernaturals for their essential materials.<br /> (Currently they have a pact with the Prince of San Francisco to keep the Sabbat contained in the South, whilst the Camarilla deal with a Hungry Dead incursion), which serves their purpose in kidnapping Sabbat Neonates).<br /> <br /> They are careful to only attack the Garou on their terms and from a position of surprise, they avoid acting against vampire elders or established mage, unless in a position of secrecy and strength and only if the benefits are worth it.<br /> <br /> Their weakness - well firstly the are horribly Wyrm tainted so family members either hole up in their fortresses or travel via dark umbra paths on rare trips, they are like a beacon to the Garou and people with low levels of true faith. Mortals feel physically sick from just being near them for short periods of time, Garou and people with higher levels of True Faith almost frenzy when encountering them.<br /> <br /> So far the Fledgling Storm Eaters impact on the Middle Umbra has confused local Garous and spirit senses, in the West.<br /> <br /> Their activities have a huge impact on the local Shadowlands attracting spectres and spawning nihils, they also provoke a similar reaction in wraiths as those with higher true faith, they utilise various rites, sorcery and the low level True Magik to conceal this in the Middle Umbra as much as possible.<br /> <br /> They have already removed the presence of family members from their Hudson Bay operation as local Faithful discovered their presence and started to disrupt their business interests.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>If I understand correctly, it's basically a mercenary family with resources involving the Wyrm and to some extent Cainite or even magical. Sounds promising to me, what kind of trouble can they cause? I understood that they have several fomori available, but I wanted to know if they have any hierarchy or pattern in the types of formori they employ.<br /> <br /> They also go after Cainites so how far do they have knowledge and resources involving Kindred? Do they have access to necromancy? Setite magic? How do they use the blood bond feature, do they bind important people in those bonds? Do they use it on Cainites, Mages, or even Garou? Do some of them decide to become ghouls or get Embraced?\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T08:48:28-07:00","id":1516975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515915-antagonist-and-enemies?p=1516953#post1516953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Red Branch </b>A group of Dauntain and Kinain, aware of their nature using their banal powers and some sorcery for their own ends, originally from Ireland with Fenian links.<br /> <br /> Some members have migrated to America to escape Fianna, Kithain and the British armies attention.<br /> Recently made a pact with the Van Bell Family for protection in the Carolina\u2019s as they rather foolishly contracted a New York gang to steal an artefact which turned out to be owned by a kindred elder.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but what ends would those specifically be, just committing crimes? And how do Dautain and Kithain manage to cooperate? I'm no expert on the subject, but as far as I know, Dautain hate Kithain, other changelins in general, and Kithain don't feel well around Dauntain, or have I misunderstood?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T11:30:06-07:00","id":1516986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515915-antagonist-and-enemies?p=1516973#post1516973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I understand correctly, it's basically a mercenary family with resources involving the Wyrm and to some extent Cainite or even magical. Sounds promising to me, what kind of trouble can they cause? I understood that they have several fomori available, but I wanted to know if they have any hierarchy or pattern in the types of formori they employ.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of trouble most of it is financial so they\u2019ll cross swords with the Ventrue, Dursirn, Grand Exchequer, in mortal terms cut throat business, bankrupting companies, liquidation driving hundreds of the poor into workhouses and destitution, as well as controlling the surrounding illicit enterprises such as loan sharking, whoring etc <br /> <br /> Formori they have several breeds notably a stalker variety that can smell vitae and hunt kindred, a form of freak feet with regeneration, enticers and hidden away monsterous formorach titans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515915-antagonist-and-enemies?p=1516973#post1516973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also go after Cainites so how far do they have knowledge and resources involving Kindred? Do they have access to necromancy? Setite magic? How do they use the blood bond feature, do they bind important people in those bonds? Do they use it on Cainites, Mages, or even Garou? Do some of them decide to become ghouls or get Embraced?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>They know a considerable amount about the kindred from torturing captured vampires, they possess necromantic paths and yes freely utilise blood bonds via captive kindred to control pawns, all in the effort to further corrupt and strike Faustian deals.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T13:21:05-07:00","id":1516991,"title":"","content":"The best way to think of the McGraths is as disciples of the Defiler Wyrm, but from a physical body horror angle (think Clive Barker horror but hidden beneath a veneer of normality). <br /> <br /> The family members number quite a few Ferectoi who appear normal but possess hidden powers as bane children and their businesses are focussed on physical depravation so factories that inflict industrial injury\u2019s, maim and kill, fur trading, strip mining etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T13:31:09-07:00","id":1516992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515915-antagonist-and-enemies?p=1516975#post1516975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but what ends would those specifically be, just committing crimes? And how do Dautain and Kithain manage to cooperate? I'm no expert on the subject, but as far as I know, Dautain hate Kithain, other changelins in general, and Kithain don't feel well around Dauntain, or have I misunderstood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anarchists and revolutionaries hence their connections to the Fenians, relic thieves and black marketeers with an unhealthy dose of black magic and dark occultism (sacrifices etc).<br /> <br /> Kinain not kithain so Fey blooded/descended mortals, essentially Winter People who are aware of the Fey (can see the dreaming etc).<br /> <br /> Their true goal is quite simply power, some of their members use this to further causes (such as fighting Victorian England as Ireland is at that time part of the Empire) but the majority just want power particularly supernatural power, so their efforts are focused on this.<br /> <br /> They primarily target the Kithain (as that\u2019s their kind and where they are most knowledgable) but seek to broaden their power base.<br /> <br /> They have rudimentary knowledge of the Fianna and some dealings with vampires, they don\u2019t understand Mage, thinking them just to be sorcerers much like themselves despairing allying with a Nephandic faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}